---
import ContentPage from '../../layouts/ContentPage.astro';
import Entry from '../../components/Entry.astro';
import ChipGroups from '../../components/ChipGroups.astro';
import { credentials, profiles, repos } from '../../data/links';

const skills = [
	{ label: 'Frontend', items: ['HTML', 'CSS', 'JavaScript', 'TypeScript', 'Vue.js', 'Astro', 'Vite', 'GSAP', 'Three.js'] },
	{
		label: 'Backend & cloud',
		items: ['Node.js', 'Firebase Auth', 'Cloud Functions', 'Firestore', 'Cloud Storage', 'PHP', 'Java', 'SQL', 'NoSQL'],
	},
	{
		label: 'CI/CD & DevOps',
		items: ['GitHub Actions', 'Firebase Hosting', 'Cloudflare Workers', 'Google Cloud Monitoring', 'Google Cloud Logging', 'Google Cloud Secret Manager'],
	},
	{ label: 'APIs & integrations', items: ['Stripe', 'Apple Wallet', 'Google Wallet', 'Twilio SendGrid & SMS', 'Google Maps'] },
	{ label: 'Testing', items: ['Playwright', 'Firebase Emulator Suite', 'Unit and integration testing'] },
	{ label: 'Design', items: ['Figma'] },
];
const NDA_NOTE = 'Private client project — available to discuss in interviews.';
---

<ContentPage
	title="Web Development"
	eyebrow="Portfolio"
	intro="Full-stack websites and web apps, from the first mockup to a monitored production deployment."
>
	<div class="prose">
		<p>
			I build complete web applications, both frontend and backend. Right now I work as a contract full-stack engineer on
			two client projects. One is a national credentialing platform with payments, digital wallet passes and automated
			testing and deployment. The other is a website redesign for a multi-location medical clinic, with a focus on search
			engine optimization.
		</p>
	</div>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Skills</h2>
		<ChipGroups groups={skills} />
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Featured work</h2>
		<p class="section-intro">Client project details are under NDA.</p>
		<div class="entry-list">
			<Entry
				title="National Credentialing & Verification Platform"
				subtitle="Contract Full-Stack Engineer"
				meta="Aug 2026 – Present"
				tags={['Cloud Functions', 'Firestore', 'Node.js', 'Stripe', 'Apple Wallet', 'Google Wallet', 'GitHub Actions', 'Playwright']}
				note={NDA_NOTE}
			>
				<p>A national registry that verifies the credentials of fitness professionals.</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Built the full stack: the frontend in plain JavaScript and Vite, and a backend made of ten Firebase Cloud
						Functions codebases.
					</li>
					<li>Built membership billing with Stripe, using webhooks to keep account status in sync with payments.</li>
					<li>
						Created digital credential passes for Apple Wallet and Google Wallet, plus a public page where anyone can verify a
						member.
					</li>
					<li>Built automated email and SMS reminders on scheduled functions, timed to each member’s time zone.</li>
					<li>
						Set up CI/CD with GitHub Actions running unit, integration and Playwright end-to-end tests, and production
						monitoring with alerts and uptime checks.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</Entry>
			<Entry
				title="Medical Clinic Website Redesign"
				subtitle="Contract Web Developer"
				meta="Oct 2026 – Present"
				tags={['HTML', 'CSS', 'SEO', 'Cloudflare Workers']}
				note={NDA_NOTE}
			>
				<p>A redesign that moves a multi-location wellness clinic off a no-code website builder.</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Developed the design through four rounds of mockups, including a brand guide and a services hub.</li>
					<li>
						Built a 15-page static site with clean URLs, a page for each location with an embedded map, and a searchable menu
						of 145 services.
					</li>
					<li>
						Implemented technical SEO: titles and descriptions written for each page, structured data (JSON-LD) and a
						sitemap.
					</li>
					<li>
						Planned permanent (301) redirects from the old site’s addresses so the clinic keeps its existing search rankings.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</Entry>
			<Entry
				title="Personal Portfolio"
				subtitle="This site"
				meta="Oct 2026 – Present"
				tags={['Astro', 'TypeScript', 'GSAP', 'Three.js']}
				links={[{ label: 'GitHub', href: repos.portfolio }]}
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="content-section">
		<h2>Education &amp; credentials</h2>
		<div class="list-card card">
			<ul class="plain-list">
				<li>
					<a href="/education">B.S. in Computer Science, Illinois State University</a> (2025): three web development courses
					with semester-long projects (IT 326, IT 353 and IT 391)
				</li>
				<li>
					Coursera:{' '}
					<a href={credentials.django} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Building Web Applications in Django</a> and{' '}
					<a href={credentials.djangoFeatures} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Django Features and Libraries</a> (University of
					Michigan)
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="cta card">
		<p>Interested in working together?</p>
		<ul class="jump-nav">
			<li><a href={profiles.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contact me on LinkedIn</a></li>
			<li><a href={profiles.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">View my GitHub</a></li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</ContentPage>
